  "paper": "foundations",
  "argument": "vectors-components",
  "title": "The length of a velocity from its components",
  "spoken": "The length of v is the square root of v x squared plus v y squared.",
  "explanation": "Pythagoras on the arrow: the two components are the sides of a right triangle and the speed is its long side.",
